→ Source generation can't optimize dynamic types; falls back to reflection-like behavior.

### ❌ Anti-Pattern 3: Many Custom Converters
Every custom converter you write becomes a bottleneck that neither library can optimize away. If your project has dozens of custom converters, the relative gain shrinks.

### ❌ Anti-Pattern 4: Streaming/Large Payloads Without Proper Handling
For multi-megabyte payloads, ensure you're using `JsonDocument` or streaming APIs in STJ, not loading everything into memory first.

