## Migration Considerations Beyond Raw Speed

| Concern | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| **API compatibility** | Medium-High | `System.Text.Json` lacks some Newtonsoft features (e.g., `DefaultValueHandling.Ignore`, certain converter patterns). Use [`Newtonsoft.Json.Bson`](https://www.nuget.org/packages/Newtonsoft.Json.Bson) or write custom converters. |
| **Custom converters** | Medium | Most Newtonsoft converters can be rewritten as `JsonConverter<T>` for STJ. Complexity varies. |
| **Null handling** | Low-Medium | STJ defaults differ (e.g., null values omitted by default in serialization unless configured). Set `DefaultIgnoreCondition = JsonIgnoreCondition.Never` if needed. |
| **Date formats** | Low | STJ uses ISO 8601 by default. Newtonsoft uses `/Date(...)/` by default. Configure via `JsonSerializerOptions`. |
| **Community ecosystem** | Low | Fewer third-party packages target STJ directly, but this is rapidly changing. |
